From: Harmony Project
Subject: x86/amd: omit the absent FCH reset-status probe on Harmony SVM

Linux's Zen late initializer reads and clears the physical FCH reset-status
register at 0xfed803c0. Harmony's virtual platform has no FCH or retained
physical reset reasons. Skip that diagnostic probe for the named SVM profile.

The extension requires compiled AMD KVM, the Harmony clock request, AMD
identity and SVM. Ordinary configurations compile it out; stock AMD boots
retain the existing reset-status probe.

This patch is Linux-kernel code (GPL-2.0), carried as a diff under the Harmony
repository's designated guest-kernel patch exception.

---
--- a/arch/x86/kernel/cpu/amd.c
+++ b/arch/x86/kernel/cpu/amd.c
@@ -13,6 +13,7 @@
 #include <asm/processor.h>
 #include <asm/apic.h>
 #include <asm/cacheinfo.h>
+#include <asm/harmony_pvclock.h>
 #include <asm/cpu.h>
 #include <asm/cpu_device_id.h>
 #include <asm/spec-ctrl.h>
@@ -1359,6 +1360,11 @@
 	u32 value;
 	int i;
 
+	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_KVM_AMD) && harmony_pvclock_requested() &&
+	    boot_cpu_data.x86_vendor == X86_VENDOR_AMD &&
+	    boot_cpu_has(X86_FEATURE_SVM))
+		return 0;
+
 	if (!cpu_feature_enabled(X86_FEATURE_ZEN))
 		return 0;
 
